#
# Counter-example for the native math:ProjectionConfidenceAsProbability gate: a
# math:ProjectionRecord declares that it converts a source confidence into a
# math:ProbabilityValue (math:projectsConfidenceAsProbability true) but names NO
# math:declaredConfidenceMapping to license the conversion. The native gate MUST emit
# math:ProjectionConfidenceAsProbability (and no other projection failure class): a
# projection may never erode the logic: probability/confidence boundary silently.
# Single violation: the confidence→probability conversion has no declared mapping. The
# record declares logic:ExactPreservation — the numeric value crosses the seam unchanged,
# so nothing is dropped and there is nothing to enumerate — which keeps the loss-ledger
# obligations (math:MissingPreservationKind, math:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct)
# satisfied and leaves the unlicensed retyping as the fixture's only defect.
# Back-reference: math:projectsConfidenceAsProbability / math:ProjectionConfidenceAsProbability (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:confidenceProjection a math:ProjectionRecord ;
    math:projectionSource ex:extractionScore ;
    math:projectionTargetName "OWL annotation (probability literal)" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:ExactPreservation ;
    math:projectsConfidenceAsProbability true .
